#main notes
A website that calculates the total gas consumption of your trip;

Features:

Gives the current gas price (updates every x hours) 
Calculates the total distance from Point A to Point B (need api)
Calculates the average total gas price based on:
how many km the trip would be
How much does the vehicle consumes gas e.g 40km/litter

The total gas price could also be divided for group trip:
Example: 
Total is 5500PHP

The trip included 6 peers

916.66PHP would be the individual pool resource

Upon research: 
(every Tuesday) → update MongoDB → Express API → React UI 


The core loop is clear: distance → fuel needed → cost → split. That's genuinely useful.

The group split feature is a great differentiator — most fuel calculators skip this entirely.

Thinking about live gas prices from the start is the right call; stale prices make the result meaningless.

Inputs you'll need from the user:
Vehicle fuel efficiency (km/L) — you have this ✓
Fuel type (unleaded, diesel, premium) — prices differ significantly
Number of passengers for the split ✓

API options worth looking into:
Distance: Google Maps Distance Matrix API or OpenRouteService (free tier) — these give real road distance, not just straight-line

Nice-to-haves for later:
Round trip toggle (doubles the distance)
Multiple stops, not just A→B
Save/share trip summary
Currency already fits PHP which is great for your market

